#: ../../update_product.md:14 eb8fc1d6a9f549dd816f0570290b1d9a
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:16 8ff71c594fe94ebf814a6e8e28877615
msgid ""
"Syncs an existing Shopify product from Airtable. **Airtable is the source"
" of truth** for everything it writes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:19 d38d52a500464ea8ab4d5f5eadcd46b4
msgid ""
"**Product:** title (`Name`), description (`Short description`), vendor "
"(`Marque`, or `Sans marque`), product type (the Type's `Name`), and "
"status (the linked \"Annonces Shopify\" record's `Status`: "
"`active`/`draft`/`archived`/`unlisted`, case ignored; left as is when "
"empty, a failure when it's anything else). An empty Airtable value never "
"clears a Shopify field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:24 69fa9d7dbd7e4458afe395a18b778387
msgid ""
"**Metafields:** the same set `create_product_shopify` writes -- "
"`long_description`, `reconditionnement`, `livraison`, `garantie`, "
"`main_table` -- plus the family \"filter\" metafields "
"(`FAMILY_FILTER_METAFIELDS`, currently only `Balances`). A filter spec "
"Airtable doesn't have is listed in `details.filter_specs_missing` (no "
"alert email -- this script runs on every stock change)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:29 f1188b8362c6498b9d820f29e0955acd
msgid ""
"**Images:** the Model's `Photo neuve`, then the `Photos marketplace` of "
"its first sellable unit that has any -- the same images "
"`create_product_shopify` uploads (see \"Images\" below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:32 5928c89de375420e9b11340b91e6087a
msgid "**Documentation PDF:** see below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:33 4b6c229bf98840be94059402af401ee8
msgid ""
"**Options and variants:** the product is reconciled to Airtable, never "
"just patched. Options: \"État esthétique\", plus the size option (the "
"Variation's `Variant_value`; label from the Type, see "
"`_variant_option_name`) whenever *any* of the Model's Variations has a "
"`Variant_value` -- with or without stock right now, since that's what "
"reconciliation matches a variant against. Variants: exactly one per "
"sellable (condition[, variant value]) combination, with Airtable's price,"
" weight and stock -- a missing one is **created**, one with nothing left "
"to sell is **deleted**. When the options change (e.g. a product created "
"without the size option), every variant is recreated under the new "
"options. Shopify requires at least one variant, so when the whole Model "
"has nothing left to sell, the existing variants are kept and **set to a "
"zero stock**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:45 0d277b3f03664134855b3d07f2cd5b56
msgid ""
"When the Model's `to_sell_on_shopify` is **\"Non\"**, the run instead "
"**deletes the Shopify product and its \"Annonces Shopify\" record** "
"(every linked one). A product already gone from Shopify (404) still has "
"its listing deleted; any other Shopify error stops before the listing is "
"deleted, so a retry still knows what to delete. An empty (or "
"unrecognized) `to_sell_on_shopify` is a failure -- deleting a live "
"product over an unfilled field would be too destructive a guess. Accepted"
" values: \"Oui\"/\"Non\" (or booleans)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:53 a38279bff330415987fe79b793ad0b1c
msgid "Two entry modes, both real (nothing here previews or dry-runs):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:55 8d9b41c8a1db4bf98ab56b161b945a07
msgid ""
"**`record_id`** (a Variation id, the default/existing convention): "
"resolves that Variation's parent Model, then updates the whole product. "
"Shopify variants all belong to one product per Model anyway, so \"update "
"one variation\" and \"update its model\" converge on the same write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:59 bd639f3fa72d4f36b06ea5459694b3c6
msgid ""
"**`model_id`**: the identical pipeline, entered directly from a Model id "
"-- what the Airtable automations use (see \"Triggering from Airtable\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:62 a51990c79daa44638c752557bfaecaef
msgid ""
"Nothing here creates a brand-new Shopify listing -- see "
"`create_product_shopify` for that. A Model with no Shopify product yet "
"(`Aucun produit Shopify associé à ce modèle`) is a validation failure "
"here, not something this script will fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:66 516dc4b1715f4fcab87ced948407bd99
msgid ""
"Like `create_product_shopify` (same `_collect_sellable_units`), it fails "
"before any Shopify write when a sellable unit (A vendre, not Abimé/Très "
"abimé) has a `Prix de vente HT` of 0, empty or invalid. The run history "
"links to that unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:70 4344dfcf379f4c95bbfe9dbbec93b564
msgid "Triggering from Airtable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:72 e9d125c312c7435a8e2f1b23da98f8ec
msgid ""
"The four automations that used to call the queue manager (\"Update fiche "
"shopify (vendus)\", \"(Pas a vendre)\", \"(modifs)\", \"Update quantité "
"shopify (entry)\") all run the same script (\"Run script\" action, input "
"`model_id` = the Model's record id), with `AIRTABLE_AUTOMATION_TOKEN`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:97 83c05398f9aa440aaa193b0f2c22001f
msgid ""
"The response only confirms the run was queued; its outcome is in `GET "
"/internal/scripts/update_product/runs` (and the alert email on failure)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:100 13c4c81358f349608738042c68116494
msgid "Images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:102 d34db622ed454e6594f75e5567857335
msgid ""
"**Source:** the Model's `Photo neuve` (all of them; missing, or any under"
" 300x300px, is a failure), then the `Photos marketplace` of the first "
"sellable unit that has any (under 300x300px or duplicating a `Photo "
"neuve` url: skipped) -- shared with `create_product_shopify` via "
"`_marketplace_photo_attachments`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:106 36fa965214c3484c89b2f530e7f0a711
msgid ""
"**Change detection:** the Airtable attachment ids the Shopify images came"
" from are recorded, in order, in the `custom.images_airtable_ids` "
"metafield. Images are replaced only when that differs from Airtable's "
"current list, or when Shopify's image count no longer matches. A product "
"whose images predate this (no recorded ids) has them replaced once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:111 fcd58da379d74f87b3eb8d9d19e24aa4
msgid ""
"**Replacement:** new images are uploaded first (in order, with their "
"position); the old ones are deleted only once every upload worked. A "
"failed upload deletes what it added and leaves the old images in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:114 e68b583bc8ee4c0ab2beb8dd7cbf2183
msgid ""
"**Worth knowing:** the marketplace photos follow the *first sellable* "
"unit -- when that unit is sold, the next one's photos replace them on the"
" next update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:117 5fe019cea07a45afab9eabe8d4b081d4
msgid "Documentation PDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:119 659ce7ceffb74b28be5a668c5bfb67a6
msgid ""
"Shared with `create_product_shopify` via "
"`api/scripts/_product_documentation.py` (upload through "
"`api/integrations/shopify_files.py`, GraphQL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:122 62b1259380484fdb973cb904f42ef3aa
msgid ""
"**Source:** the Model's Airtable `Documentation` attachment field -- the "
"first attachment that is a PDF (MIME type, or a `.pdf` filename). Other "
"attachments are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:124 0b8be7a18fb24444ab72d710f9f90b91
msgid ""
"**Target:** the product metafield "
"`SHOPIFY_PDF_METAFIELD_NAMESPACE`.`SHOPIFY_PDF_METAFIELD_KEY` (default "
"`custom.pdf_descriptif`, the \"PDF Descriptif\" definition), type "
"`file_reference`, plus a companion `single_line_text_field` "
"(`custom.pdf_descriptif_airtable_id` by default) recording the Airtable "
"attachment id the Shopify file came from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:128 75b8608ca777445290fa03b53cd2d9eb
msgid ""
"**Upload:** the PDF is downloaded from Airtable (signed url, fetched "
"fresh with the record) and sent through Shopify's staged upload -> "
"`fileCreate` -> poll until `READY` -> `metafieldsSet` (both metafields in"
" one atomic call)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:131 82f603363add41e499f0d95448aa28e8
msgid ""
"**Change detection:** same \"diff against live Shopify\" approach as the "
"rest of `update_product` -- no extra state store (the two metafields are "
"read through GraphQL first). Upload when Shopify has no PDF, or when the "
"recorded source id differs from Airtable's current attachment id "
"(Airtable gives a replaced file a new id). A Shopify PDF set by hand "
"before this sync existed has no source id, so it is replaced once by "
"Airtable's, then stays stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:137 dcc02db867464f72ad08a3faa0664561
msgid ""
"**Never clears:** an empty Airtable field writes nothing "
"(`documentation_status: \"absent\"`) -- there's no deletion-sync "
"convention in this project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:139 cd2317356207415caabc28aca700c772
msgid ""
"**Size limit:** a PDF over Shopify's 20 MB limit is first compressed with"
" Ghostscript (`api/utils/pdf_compression.py`); if it's still too big, the"
" sync fails with both sizes in the message (the Airtable original is "
"never modified)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:142 943e63875aab47eab4862100d95d21f3
msgid ""
"The replaced Shopify file is not deleted from the Files library (it may "
"be referenced elsewhere)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:144 b06d75f886564bb1ba6845aa778cce6d
msgid ""
"**Scopes:** the Shopify app needs `write_files` and `read_files` "
"(confirmed missing on the RewakeDev token on 2026-09-28 -- `fileCreate` "
"answers ACCESS_DENIED without them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:146 151423eb6e9a466f8087a43b708e1c44
msgid ""
"**Failure handling:** runs inside the per-Model lock, after variants. A "
"failed upload doesn't stop the rest of the sync, but turns the run into a"
" `failure` afterwards (same rule as a failed variant creation: it's what "
"reconciliation's documentation bulk action runs this script for)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:151 87bf1817cd7346f7beaee0e00840d5b8
msgid "Locking: runs for one Model never overlap, and never get dropped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:153 80ad1a5642184565921bc69d28e971ba
msgid ""
"The per-`record_id` Redis lock in `api/tasks.py` (shared by every script)"
" guards the outer request layer -- keyed by whatever the caller passed in"
" as `record_id`. `update_product` sets `requeue_when_locked`, so a run "
"that finds it held is put back on the queue instead of being skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:157 d11b47b5a94c4325bd9525630e48f988
msgid ""
"A second lock, acquired inside `run()` once the Model is resolved, keyed "
"by the Model id (`RunStore.acquire_lock(\"update_product_model\", "
"model_id)`, the `SHOPIFY_MODEL_LOCK_NAME` of "
"`api/scripts/_shopify_links.py`) -- the one that actually matters, since "
"a Variation id and a Model id (or two Variations of one Model) resolve to"
" the same Shopify product. `create_product_shopify` takes the same lock, "
"so an update never runs while the product is still being created. A run "
"that finds it held raises `RequeueLater`, and `api/tasks.py` puts it back"
" on the queue (5s countdown, up to `REQUEUE_MAX_RETRIES` = 120 times, "
"then a `failure` run is recorded)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:166 8f832500d53e4053904b103d7b6194a8
msgid ""
"Every Airtable read happens after the Model lock is acquired, with a "
"fresh cache -- a run that waited its turn syncs Airtable's *latest* "
"state, not what it saw when it was triggered. A waiting run isn't "
"recorded in the run history; only the run that actually happens is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:171 184b5b76bcee4d5da1d85b5b61ac54e8
msgid "Data it touches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:191 b099ee03b729441cbbc7c2584cb625d7
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:193 af89a5156c474363949e0c4b84feee80
msgid ""
"Resolve the Model: `record_id` mode verifies the id really belongs to the"
" `Variation` table (Airtable's single-record GET doesn't validate that --"
" see `_assert_belongs_to_table`), then reads its `Model` link field; "
"`model_id` mode verifies the id belongs to `Model` directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:197 9699c1cc9a5a4f2584ea47638a970591
msgid "Acquire the per-Model lock (or requeue -- see above), then read the Model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:198 87f626d7b78441678d5bb299b2f4b981
msgid ""
"`to_sell_on_shopify` = \"Non\": delete the Shopify product(s) and "
"listing(s), done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:199 8f1830b5ac044fddb61d47f5e617ad9d
msgid ""
"Validate: a Shopify product is linked (via `Annonces Shopify` -> "
"`ID_shopify`, the same `_resolve_listing_ids` helper "
"`create_product_shopify.py` uses), the listing's `Status` is valid, the "
"Type is set and exists, the weight (when set) is a number -- an empty "
"weight just leaves the variants' weight alone. Collect the sellable units"
" with the same `_collect_sellable_units`/`_build_variant_rows` helpers "
"`create_product_shopify.py` uses (`api/scripts/_shopify_links.py`, so "
"both scripts agree on what the variants *should* be) -- an empty result "
"is fine here: it means zero stock everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:207 58bea9fad7034aba8b4404208da34174
msgid ""
"Fetch the live product, then sync, in this order: variants (stock first "
"-- it's what matters most if anything later fails), product fields, "
"metafields, documentation PDF, images. Each step diffs against the live "
"product first -- a no-op write is never sent. Variants go through one "
"product PUT with the full variant list (Shopify REST: a listed variant "
"with an `id` is kept and updated, one without is created, an unlisted one"
" is deleted) -- which is also what lets the options themselves change -- "
"then each variant's stock is pushed. A variant's identity is its option "
"values, stripped, in position order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:215 d3460fe6b9a74f9682a422c28e0aa485
msgid ""
"A failure in any step is collected, not fatal: every other step still "
"runs, then the run reports `status=\"failure\"` with every reason (first "
"5 in `details.error`) and the partial progress (the details and metrics "
"below, merged into `details`). A missing/invalid `Photo neuve` works the "
"same way: images are skipped, everything else syncs, the run fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:220 0099640b126f4258a1c1ba2ced87e63b
msgid ""
"Live stages (`GET /internal/scripts/update_product/current`): "
"`resolving_variation` or `resolving_model`, `validating_model`, then "
"either `removing_from_shopify` or `validating_stock`, "
"`fetching_shopify_product`, `syncing_variants`, `syncing_product`, "
"`syncing_metafields`, `syncing_documentation`, `syncing_images`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:225 cf4ecb26292241b1bc280bdb66d1fa81
msgid "Deliberate deviations from the source (`Update-Product`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:227 20817625d4ba4a758a3d21134126affe
msgid ""
"**Queued, not skipped, when busy.** An earlier version of this port "
"skipped a run that found the product's lock held (`status=\"skipped\"`) "
"-- but that run could be the one carrying the newer Airtable data (a sale"
" triggering two automations at once), so it now waits its turn instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:231 cd7e52cbfce64f57811116402f7d6c61
msgid ""
"**In-process, no subprocess.** The source shelled out to `uv run Update-"
"Product/main.py <record_id>`, parsing captured stdout/stderr to guess "
"success (`stderr == \"\"`) -- unreliable, since `Update-Product` logs "
"structured JSON events to stderr *by design*, even on a clean run. This "
"port sidesteps that signal entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:236 1913a89b9d2547f98bb47240052af8fc
msgid ""
"**No sandbox/dry-run mode.** The source defaulted to a sandbox mode "
"(reads real data, logs what it *would* do, never actually writes) unless "
"an `ENVIRONMENT`/`ENV` var said \"prod\". This port always writes for "
"real once triggered, matching `create_product_shopify`'s own behavior and"
" this codebase's existing posture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:240 b0b033964b61454cae0c85c3638a2277
msgid ""
"**No `ALLOW_VARIANT_CREATE` permission gate.** The source required an "
"explicit opt-in env var before it would create a missing variant, "
"defaulting to blocking that. This port always creates a missing variant "
"-- a routine, expected part of \"update\", not an edge case to guard "
"against (this is also exactly what makes reconciliation's \"Variations "
"absentes de Shopify\" -> \"Mettre à jour\" button meaningful)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:245 46bd508ff4d941149b958d0432a3382d
msgid ""
"**REST, not GraphQL, for every Shopify write.** The source used Shopify's"
" GraphQL Admin API (`productUpdate`, `metafieldsSet`, "
"`productVariantsBulkUpdate`, `productVariantsBulkCreate`) plus one REST "
"inventory call. This port extends the existing REST-only `ShopifyAdmin` "
"(`api/integrations/shopify_rest.py`) instead of introducing a second, "
"GraphQL-based client alongside it -- one consistent Shopify integration "
"style for both scripts, same asymmetric retry semantics (see that "
"module's own docstring), same positional option/variant matching "
"`create_product_shopify.py`'s own `_create_variants` already established."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:253 40e5daec494042f395e02c4e38a3c093
msgid ""
"**Inventory location: the existing `SHOPIFY_LOCATION_ID` constant, not a "
"live lookup.** The source queried Shopify for \"the first location\" on "
"every run (`locations(first: 1)`) and used whatever came back. This port "
"reuses the already-configured `SHOPIFY_LOCATION_ID` (set up for "
"`create_product_shopify`) -- the dev store alone has 3 locations, so "
"\"whichever one Shopify lists first\" is a real correctness risk the "
"source carried, not something worth preserving."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:259 1db2f24e106b4bce9551bc68846b1113
msgid ""
"**A single `_ValidationFailed` exception, not the source's 9-class "
"hierarchy.** `Update-Product/errors.py`'s granular exceptions "
"(`RecordNotInVariationTableError`, `NoUnitsLinkedError`, `NoPriceError`, "
"etc.) map 1:1 to specific checks, but `create_product_shopify.py` already"
" established a single internal exception (message + `extra_details` for "
"Airtable links) as this codebase's own convention for exactly this kind "
"of \"one of several checks failed\" flow. This port follows that "
"precedent rather than introducing a second error-handling philosophy "
"alongside it -- each check still raises a distinct, specific message, "
"just not a distinct class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:267 a58ec631c69e415b8dfd46c764e0de5e
msgid ""
"**Alerts via the existing Gmail API service, not raw SMTP.** The source "
"sent alert emails via `smtplib` and a Gmail app password "
"(`SMTP_GMAIL_PASSWORD`) -- the same category of credential exposure "
"flagged in `Update-Product/docs/incident-2026-08-shopify-duplicates.md`'s"
" security remediation checklist. This port reuses "
"`api/services/gmail.py`'s `send_alert_email` (Gmail API + a service "
"account), exactly like `create_product_shopify.py` already does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:273 0ad29af0d2044408bbb2a0301c84cf11
msgid ""
"**This port is the incident doc's own target architecture.** That "
"document's \"architecture cible\" diagram explicitly names bringing this "
"logic in-process behind an authenticated internal endpoint, with a per-"
"Shopify-id lock and no silent-success masking of a real failure -- this "
"is that migration, not an unrelated refactor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:278 77ef9e6c621e48daba6159008a929002
msgid "Known risks / things worth reviewing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:280 fafebadf5b524fb48246a575c66413d9
msgid ""
"**A model_id-mode (or a Model's *other* Variations') update isn't "
"attributed back to an individual Variation in reconciliation's cross-"
"reference.** `attach_update_attempts` in "
"`shopify_catalog_reconciliation.py` only matches a stored "
"`update_product` run against `variations_missing_in_shopify` via that "
"run's own `record_id` -- a run triggered by `model_id` (or by a "
"*different* sibling Variation of the same Model) has no `record_id` of "
"its own to match on, so it won't show up as \"already tried\" against a "
"Variation it may well have actually updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:287 f040f2744813499687951a0bda13810b
msgid ""
"**Fixed: a product created without the size option could never get it.** "
"Confirmed live (dev store, \"RT PCR Thermo Scientific QuantStudio 5\"): "
"`create_product_shopify` only added the size option when more than one "
"size had stock at creation, and `update_product` read the option count "
"from the live product, so its \"0.1 mL / Très bon\" row matched the "
"existing condition-only \"Très bon\" variant and every run reported "
"success without changing anything -- while reconciliation kept listing "
"\"0.1 mL\" as missing. Both scripts now decide the options from Airtable "
"(`_model_has_variant_values`), and update restructures a product whose "
"options differ. Worth knowing: a product whose option names differ from "
"what Airtable implies (e.g. renamed by hand) has all its variants "
"recreated once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:297 0b469524eccf490da78438cc1fbdab57
msgid ""
"**Option 1 is always \"État esthétique\".** Variants are matched by "
"option values in position order under the options Airtable implies; a "
"live product whose option names differ (an older or hand-edited one) "
"isn't matched value by value -- all its variants are recreated once, with"
" new variant ids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:301 201a4bea0c3a4b0dba7a45fde72c7bb5
msgid ""
"~~First real end-to-end verification against the dev store is still "
"pending~~ -- done: both entry modes and the reconciliation buttons were "
"run live against the dev store, which is exactly what caught the bug "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:304 4ff2a546b0464154bfd3af6c62638274
msgid ""
"**Fixed, but worth knowing about: variant option values must be compared "
"stripped, not raw.** Confirmed live: Airtable's `Variant_value` can carry"
" incidental trailing whitespace (`\"120x47 \"`) that Shopify itself trims"
" on save (`\"120x47\"`). Comparing the raw, untrimmed Airtable value "
"against Shopify's own (already-trimmed) option values meant an already-"
"existing variant was never recognized as a match -- `update_product` "
"would then attempt to create a *duplicate* variant with the same option "
"combination, which Shopify correctly rejects, and (before this fix) that "
"rejection was silently logged and swallowed, with the run still reporting"
" `status=\"success\"`. Both bugs are now fixed: `_variant_key` (used for "
"both the Airtable rows and the live Shopify variants) strips both sides "
"before comparing, and a failed variant *creation* now makes the whole run"
" report `status=\"failure\"` (with the real Shopify rejection reason in "
"`details.error`) instead of silently succeeding. Since then, every "
"variant sync failure (price, weight, stock, zero stock) does the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../update_product.md:317 4401df0fef5944038325889acd1258d5
msgid ""
"**A `requests.Response` is falsy for any non-2xx status** "
"(`Response.__bool__` returns `self.ok`) -- code that checks `if response "
"else None` instead of `if response is not None else None` silently "
"discards the real status code/body of a genuine error response. This "
"exact mistake is what hid the bug above during initial testing (logs "
"showed `\"status\": null` for a real 422). Fixed via "
"`_response_error_detail`, which checks `is not None` and includes the "
"actual response body. Worth grepping for this same `if response else ...`"
" pattern if it's ever copied elsewhere."
msgstr ""

